# Nothing in here is needed to serve the site, and everything in here was
# being published at a public URL because Vercel deploys the whole repo.
# It all stays in git. It just stops being downloadable from 4ormiq.com.

# Build and verification tooling
tools/

# Internal documentation and the change register. admin.html embeds the
# register at build time, so it is not fetched at runtime.
docs/

# THE BACK OFFICE. Excluding docs/ protected the register as a file and did
# nothing for the register as embedded text: audit-embed.mjs writes it into
# admin.html, and admin.html was deployed. The page is a static asset, so
# Vercel served all 731KB of it to anybody who asked, with the whole change
# register inside, CR-0013's four open items among them, the ten control
# standards with their NO-GO states and the release posture. The Clerk check
# on that page is client-side: it decides what is DRAWN, not what is SENT.
# There is no middleware in this repository, so nothing refused the bytes.
#
# A file excluded and a page carrying the same text deployed are the same
# disclosure with different plumbing. tools/deploycheck.mjs is now the gate.
#
# TO PUT THE BACK OFFICE BACK ON THE WEB, one of these first, then delete
# this line:
#   turn on Vercel Deployment Protection for the project, which refuses the
#     request before the file is served, or
#   stop embedding the register and read it from /api/audit, which is gated.
# Until then it opens as a local file, which is what the embed was for.
admin.html

# Schema, applied by hand against the database
db/

# Internal reports and their PDFs
reports/

# Superseded pages, kept for history
archive/

# Decks and plans. These are not web pages.
*.pptx
*.pdf

node_modules/
.env
.env.*

# Audits. Internal.
audits/
